\fs44\b Pest and Crop Disease Detection\par
\fs36 System Analysis Report (Current State)\b0\par
\fs24\par
\fs24 Project workspace: clean-repo\par
\fs24 Date: 2026-04-16\par
\fs24\par
\pard\sa200
\fs28\b 1. Executive Status\b0\par
\fs24 Current release readiness is BLOCKED for field deployment under strict policy.\par
\fs24 Lab and test metrics are strong for the 15-class model, but field supported-confident coverage is below required thresholds for all supported crops.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 2. Problem Definition\b0\par
\fs24 Smallholder farmers need fast, trustworthy disease triage in low-connectivity environments. The key problem is not only prediction accuracy, but also safe rejection of unsupported crops and uncertain cases without creating harmful false confidence.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 3. Stakeholders and Success Criteria\b0\par
\fs24 - Smallholder farmers: require simple offline diagnosis and clear next-step advice.\par
\fs24 - Extension officers: require reliable and interpretable outputs during field visits.\par
\fs24 - Project owner/researcher: requires measurable deployment readiness, not only high lab accuracy.\par
\fs24 - Maintainer/developer: requires reproducible training, threshold control, and release governance.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 4. Functional Architecture (Implemented)\b0\par
\fs24 - Mobile app captures image from camera or gallery.\par
\fs24 - Image passes quality and risk gates before final classification claim.\par
\fs24 - TFLite model runs fully on-device (offline-first).\par
\fs24 - Multi-gate classifier pipeline applies G5/G5b/G7* safety checks and crop-aware rescue logic for beans/potato edge cases.\par
\fs24 - Results and scan history are persisted locally (SQLite).\par
\fs24 - Runtime thresholds are loaded from app asset config with safe defaults.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 5. Non-Functional State\b0\par
\fs24 - Offline operation: achieved.\par
\fs24 - On-device performance: architecture is suitable for low-to-mid Android hardware.\par
\fs24 - Deployment packaging: signed release APK exists (75.3 MB).\par
\fs24 - Safety posture: conservative, with uncertainty/unsupported rejection prioritized.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 6. Data and Model State\b0\par
\fs24 - Model configuration indicates 15 classes including other_leaf.\par
\fs24 - Test evaluation (15-class): accuracy 0.945, macro F1 0.9352, other_leaf recall 0.9829.\par
\fs24 - Crop confusion safety metrics satisfy strict limits (beans/potato and supported/unsupported confusion all within policy caps).\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 7. Field Validation State (Critical)\b0\par
\fs24 Strict release policy requires supported_confident_rate >= 0.80 per crop.\par
\fs24 Measured field supported_confident_rate values:\par
\fs24 - banana: 0.5556\par
\fs24 - beans: 0.4000\par
\fs24 - maize: 0.3750\par
\fs24 - potato: 0.6923\par
\fs24 Therefore release verdict is BLOCKED (all four crops below requirement).\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 8. Gate-Level Behavioral Analysis\b0\par
\fs24 Field audits show many samples ending as uncertain or unsupported despite acceptable confusion safety. This indicates conservative thresholds and gate interactions are limiting supported confident coverage in real-photo conditions.\par
\fs24 Rescue gates improve beans/potato outcomes in several cases, but current settings are still insufficient to pass strict per-crop acceptance targets.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 9. Configuration Governance Risks\b0\par
\fs24 Multiple threshold artifacts exist from calibration and pilot tuning sessions (calibration outputs, deployment manifest notes, and runtime asset config).\par
\fs24 This creates drift risk unless one source of truth is enforced per release candidate and validated end-to-end with readiness scripts.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 10. Constraints and Limitations\b0\par
\fs24 - Scope limited to supported crops and disease classes in training data.\par
\fs24 - Real-world image variability remains the dominant deployment challenge.\par
\fs24 - High safety settings may reduce false positives but increase uncertain/unsupported outcomes on valid crops.\par
\fs24 - The system is decision support, not a replacement for agronomic diagnosis in complex cases.\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 11. Feasibility Reassessment\b0\par
\fs24 - Technical feasibility: high (pipeline, model, app, gating, and diagnostics are mature).\par
\fs24 - Operational feasibility: medium (requires threshold stabilization and successful field acceptance against policy).\par
\fs24 - Deployment feasibility now: conditional (NO-GO until strict field gate passes).\par
\fs24\par
\fs28\b 12. Immediate Recommendations\b0\par
\fs24 1) Re-run strict real-photo field audit on the exact runtime thresholds planned for release.\par
\fs24 2) Apply only controlled threshold tuning within the allowed hotfix window, then re-validate release readiness.\par
\fs24 3) If still blocked, expand hard examples for low-coverage crops and retrain before attempting release.\par
\fs24 4) Complete device install and offline smoke tests, then update deployment records.\par
}